# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Private project materials: official register maps, generated catalog data,
# internal specifications, and agent instructions remain local only.
#
# /docs/ itself is deliberately NOT ignored as a whole directory — git
# cannot "un-ignore" individual files inside an ignored directory (a
# documented limitation: it never descends into one to check exceptions),
# so the two actually-private documents are named directly instead. Task 8's
# own deliverables (docs/README.md, docs/point-reference.md,
# docs/open-questions.md) are generated *output* or a plain operator guide,
# not internal specs or raw register-map data — same "generated output is
# tracked" convention gen/ already uses — and stay tracked normally.
/m261-registermap/
/catalog/point_catalog.json
/catalog/validation_report.md
/docs/AGENT-TASK.md
/docs/AGENT-CODE-REVIEW.md

# Credentials and local runtime configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
secrets/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Go
/simulator/**/*.exe
/simulator/bin/

# OS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: generated code in gen/ is intentionally tracked, not ignored.
.venv/
